 bridges:{title:'Bridges & connectors',category:'connect',icon:'link',tag:'Reuse existing investments',short:'Make existing APIs and agents accessible to the network.',simple:'An adapter can help a capability join the ecosystem without rebuilding the underlying system.',technical:'MCP Bridge exposes selected existing API operations as MCP tools. MCP Connector supports custom Mule server/client logic. A2A Bridge adapts supported non-A2A agents; A2A Connector enables Mule-based agent communication.',example:'Expose a permitted order lookup operation as a tool while leaving the order system in place.',value:'Bring enterprise capabilities into agentic workflows incrementally.',note:'The correct integration depends on the source system, supported interfaces, authentication, and required transformations.',source:'bridge',extraSource:'a2abridge',map:'toolA'},
 costs:{title:'Model policies & cost',category:'govern',icon:'coins',tag:'Control model usage',short:'Apply relevant safeguards and usage limits to LLM traffic.',simple:'Model calls consume resources. Manage their usage and apply appropriate safety controls rather than treating them as unlimited.',technical:'Gateway LLM policies include token-based rate limits and supported content or PII controls. Apply compatible policies to the configured model-proxy traffic.',example:'Use an appropriate model and limit token usage for a workload, rather than giving every request unconstrained resources.',value:'Balance useful intelligence with operating cost and risk.',note:'There are no measured costs or savings in this demo. Policy availability and compatibility vary; controls do not guarantee perfect model behavior.',source:'policies',map:'llm'},
