 systems:{title:'Your existing systems',category:'connect',icon:'cloud',tag:'Where business work happens',short:'The applications and APIs behind the useful capabilities.',simple:'Orders, employee records, and cases still live in your business systems. Agents work through permitted integrations to read or update them.',technical:'Tool implementations connect to APIs and applications. They must handle authentication, validation, errors, and any required transaction or approval logic.',example:'A create_case tool writes a real service record only when the backing integration succeeds.',value:'Make agents useful by connecting them to actual business actions.',note:'An assistant saying "done" is not proof of a successful action. Use the integration result and appropriate verification.',source:'bridge',map:'toolB'},
 user:{title:'A person or application',category:'orchestrate',icon:'user',tag:'The starting point',short:'A business goal starts the request.',simple:'A person or application asks for an outcome. The network then works within its configured capabilities and permissions.',technical:'For this example, an application sends a request to a protected broker endpoint with the required caller context. The sequence is conceptual, not a wire-level protocol trace.',example:'"Where is my order, and can you make it right?" expresses the goal without specifying every system call.',value:'Keep the customer focused on the outcome, not the integrations behind it.',note:'All people, records, messages, and results in this demonstration are fictional.',source:'network',map:'user'}
